BrainHem Assist — Baseline S publication snapshot

The project owner publishes the original code, Baseline S model artifacts and
architecture diagram without selecting an open-source license. LICENSE grants
no blanket rights to those original contributions. Third-party portions retain
their own licenses and notices.

The application integrates React, NiiVue, FastAPI and other dependencies.
Their copyrights and license terms remain with their respective owners.

mvp/frontend/scripts/patch-niivue-outline.mjs contains and modifies a NiiVue
shader fragment. Preserve LICENSES/NiiVue.txt (BSD-2-Clause) when distributing
this fragment or a bundle containing it.

This snapshot includes Baseline S in two inference formats:
models/baseline_s.onnx (FP32) and models/baseline_s.int8.onnx (mixed precision).
The latter is derived from the former by scripts/quantize_model.py and
adds no new license grant. Both formats expose graph topology, operators and
learned weights. Model slots M and L have no implementation or artifacts in
this snapshot.

Upstream source-lineage references are retained in LICENSES/model-provenance/
and described in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. Historical imports for these references
remain unconfirmed; their inclusion does not assign an upstream license to the
complete ONNX artifact. Applicable third-party terms remain in force for any
covered portions.

No medical scan volumes, private model source, local account information or
prior private Git history are included. The application capture displays the
real CT_Electrodes demonstration sample distributed by NiiVue from Seg3DData.
Preserve LICENSES/Seg3DData.txt for the sample image attribution.
The additional AI Studio images are original project UI captures from the
report and the monitor of a completed research training run. They document
the research deployment; its training runtime is not bundled here.
Existing source comments and upstream notices have been retained.
